Description: vo_gpu, vo_gpu_next: hand a 3D video's views over at their own resolution
 .
 The video layer of a 3D video was twice the window's width, and each
 view was scaled into its half at the window's size, so the compositor
 received views the renderer had already resized: a half top-and-bottom
 1920x1080 video went as two 1920x1080 views to a full screen window,
 stretched from 1920x540.
 .
 vo_get_stereo_layer() measures the window in the view's own samples:
 the layer still covers the window, its letterbox counted in samples,
 and each view is drawn into its half at the resolution it has, so the
 renderer only copies it. The viewport, which has the window's size,
 gives the compositor the one resize; that video goes as one 3840x540
 layer to a full screen window. A layer larger than a texture can be
 (16384) keeps the window's size as before.
